From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] winspool: Fail Unix calls cleanly when the printer backend
 is missing.

The console runtime has no winspool Unix library (winspool.prx: there is
no CUPS on the PS5), so __wine_init_unix_call() fails and the module's
Unix-call handle stays zero. DllMain still loads the system printers, and
its first UNIX_CALL(enum_printers) went through that zero handle: every
game start logged a syscall fault in ntdll at address 8. UNIX_CALL now
returns STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND when there is no handle, so the existing
fallbacks (no system printers, default PPD paths) run as on a system
without CUPS. With a backend present nothing changes.
---
 dlls/winspool.drv/wspool.h | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winspool.drv/wspool.h b/dlls/winspool.drv/wspool.h
index 29a459e..9de545c 100644
--- a/dlls/winspool.drv/wspool.h
+++ b/dlls/winspool.drv/wspool.h
@@ -64,7 +64,11 @@ struct get_ppd_params
     const WCHAR *ppd;
 };
 
-#define UNIX_CALL( func, params ) WINE_UNIX_CALL( unix_ ## func, params )
+/* The Windows module remains usable without its optional Unix printer
+ * backend. Return an ordinary failure instead of dispatching through a
+ * zero Unix-call handle, so the existing printer/PPD fallbacks can run. */
+#define UNIX_CALL( func, params ) \
+    (__wine_unixlib_handle ? WINE_UNIX_CALL( unix_ ## func, params ) : (NTSTATUS)STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND)
 
 enum cups_funcs
 {
